INPUT DEFINITIONS
Six supplied definitions were available and no other lesson text was consulted.
D1: Polynomial degree is the largest sum of exponents in a nonzero monomial
    after collecting terms into standard polynomial form.
D2: Equation degree is that of the standard polynomial on the left when
    the right side is zero.
D3: A pair solving a two-variable equation makes the equation a true equality.
D4: A relation graph is exactly the plane set of all solution pairs.
D5: ax+by=c with at least one nonzero coefficient is a line; a quadratic
    function with nonzero quadratic coefficient is a parabola; xy=k with
    k nonzero is a hyperbola.
D6: For positive r, x^2+y^2=r^2 is the circle centered at the origin with
    radius r. The r=0 case must instead be solved directly as a point.

